    area: android
    summary: Flutter's Gradle plugin now fails the build for Gradle below 8.14, AGP below 8.11.1 and KGP below 2.2.20, and warns below Gradle 9.1.0, AGP 9.0.1 and KGP 2.3.20.
    use: "In `android/settings.gradle.kts`: `id(\"com.android.application\") version \"9.1.0\"`, `id(\"org.jetbrains.kotlin.android\") version \"2.4.0\"`; Gradle wrapper `gradle-9.3.1-all.zip`."
    avoid: "AGP below 8.11.1 (e.g. `8.7.0`), Gradle below 8.14, or KGP below 2.2.20 (e.g. 2.0/2.1) copied from older projects; these now fail during configuration (AGP 8.11.1+ and Gradle 8.14+ only warn)."
    source: https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/3.47.5/packages/flutter_tools/gradle/src/main/kotlin/DependencyVersionChecker.kt

  - id: dart-final-var-parameters-reserved
    since: "3.47"
    languageVersion: "3.13"
    priority: 1
    area: dart
    summary: At language version 3.13, `final` and `var` on ordinary (non-declaring) parameters are a compile-time error; Dart reserves them for primary-constructor declaring parameters.
    use: "Plain parameters: `void f(int x)`, `(BuildContext context) => ...`; enable the `parameter_assignments` lint to prevent reassignment."
    avoid: "`void f(final int x)`, `(final BuildContext context) {}`, `final` or `var` on method, function, closure or in-body constructor parameters."
    source: https://github.com/dart-lang/sdk/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md#3130

  - id: ios-minimum-15
    since: "3.47"
    priority: 1
    area: ios
    summary: Flutter's minimum supported iOS is now 15 (iOS 14 and earlier are unsupported); new projects use IPHONEOS_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET 15.0 and the tool migrates older targets to 15.0.
    use: "`IPHONEOS_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET = 15.0`, Podfile `platform :ios, '15.0'`, plugin podspec `s.platform = :ios, '15.0'`."
    avoid: "`platform :ios, '13.0'` / `'12.0'`, deployment target 13.0 or 14.0, or podspecs declaring iOS 13."
    source: https://docs.flutter.dev/reference/supported-platforms

  - id: android-builtin-kotlin-version-check
    since: "3.47"
    priority: 2
    area: android
    summary: "Flutter 3.47 allows `android.builtInKotlin=true`, but on 3.47.x stable the Kotlin version check rejects AGP's bundled Kotlin 2.2.10 (issue #192167, closed by PR #192206 on master; the fix is in 3.49 beta, not in any 3.47.x stable)."
    use: "On 3.47.x keep the template's `android.builtInKotlin=false`; if you must enable built-in Kotlin, build with `--android-skip-build-dependency-validation`."
    avoid: "Setting `android.builtInKotlin=true` and removing `org.jetbrains.kotlin.android` on 3.47.x, then expecting the build to pass Flutter's KGP check."
    source: https://github.com/flutter/flutter/issues/192167

  - id: android-template-agp-9
    since: "3.47"
    priority: 2
    area: android
    summary: New Android projects are generated with Gradle 9.3.1, AGP 9.1.0 and KGP 2.4.0 (3.44 used Gradle 9.1.0, AGP 9.0.1, KGP 2.3.20).
    use: "Match the template: Gradle `9.3.1`, AGP `9.1.0`, KGP `2.4.0`, Java 17, `kotlin { compilerOptions { jvmTarget = org.jetbrains.kotlin.gradle.dsl.JvmTarget.JVM_17 } }`."
    avoid: "Hard-coding older template versions (AGP 8.x, Gradle 8.x) in new projects."
    source: https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/3.47.5/packages/flutter_tools/lib/src/android/gradle_utils.dart

  - id: dart-primary-constructors
    since: "3.47"
    languageVersion: "3.13"
    priority: 2
    area: dart
    summary: Dart 3.13 adds primary constructors, declaring a constructor and its fields in the class header.
    use: "`class Point(final int x, final int y);`; initializer list or body via `this : assert(x >= 0) { ... }` inside the class; `class const P(final int x);` for const."
    avoid: "Using primary-constructor syntax in packages whose SDK constraint lower bound is below 3.13 (`sdk: '^3.13.0'` is required)."
    source: https://dart.dev/language/primary-constructors

  - id: macos-minimum-12
    since: "3.47"
    priority: 2
    area: ios
    summary: Flutter's minimum supported macOS is now 12 (Monterey); new projects use MACOSX_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET 12.0 and the tool migrates older targets.
    use: "`MACOSX_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET = 12.0`, Podfile `platform :osx, '12.0'`, podspec `s.osx.deployment_target = '12.0'`."
    avoid: "`platform :osx, '10.15'` or `'11.0'`, deployment target 10.15."
    source: https://docs.flutter.dev/reference/supported-platforms

  - id: material-ui-packages
    since: "3.47"
    priority: 2
    area: framework
    summary: Material and Cupertino are published as standalone packages `material_ui` and `cupertino_ui`; the in-framework libraries are frozen and scheduled for formal deprecation in a later stable, but are not deprecated in 3.47.
    use: "To opt in: `flutter pub add material_ui cupertino_ui`, then `dart fix --apply --code=migrate_design_widgets`; imports become `package:material_ui/material_ui.dart` / `package:cupertino_ui/cupertino_ui.dart`."
    avoid: "Claiming `package:flutter/material.dart` is deprecated in 3.47, or expecting new Material/Cupertino features to land in the in-framework libraries."
    source: https://docs.flutter.dev/release/breaking-changes/material-ui-and-cupertino-ui

  - id: semantics-heading-level
    since: "3.47"
    priority: 2
    area: framework
    summary: The `header` semantics flag is now a no-op on iOS and Android; headings are announced only when `headingLevel` is greater than 0.
    use: "`Semantics(headingLevel: 1, child: Text('Section'))`; `SemanticsProperties(headingLevel: 1)`."
    avoid: "`Semantics(header: true, ...)` to mark headings for TalkBack/VoiceOver."
    source: https://docs.flutter.dev/release/breaking-changes/semantics-header-heading-level

  - id: dart-concise-constructor-syntax
    since: "3.47"
    languageVersion: "3.13"
    priority: 3
    area: dart
    summary: In Dart 3.13 constructors in a class body can use `new` or `factory` instead of repeating the class name.
    use: "`new(this.x, this.y);`, `new origin() : x = 0, y = 0;`, `factory clone(Point other) => Point(other.x, other.y);`"
    avoid: "This syntax below language version 3.13; a method named `factory` with no return type (`factory () {}`) now parses as an unnamed factory constructor."
    source: https://dart.dev/language/constructors

  - id: impeller-desktop-default
    since: "3.47"
    priority: 3
    area: framework
    summary: Impeller is the default renderer on macOS, Windows and Linux; the opt-out will be removed in a future release.
    use: "Assume Impeller on desktop; to opt out temporarily use `flutter run --no-enable-impeller`, `FLTEnableImpeller=false` (macOS Info.plist), `set_impeller_switch(flutter::ImpellerSwitch::Disabled)` (Windows), `fl_dart_project_set_enable_impeller(project, FALSE)` (Linux)."
    avoid: "Assuming desktop renders with Skia, or relying on the opt-out long term."
    source: https://docs.flutter.dev/perf/impeller

  - id: material-ui-bridge-limitation
    since: "3.47"
    priority: 3
    area: framework
    summary: "`MaterialUiCompatibilityBridge` passes theme and localizations to dependencies still on `package:flutter/material.dart`, but cannot fix type mismatches when a dependency's API takes or returns in-framework Material types."
    use: "`MaterialApp(builder: (context, child) => MaterialUiCompatibilityBridge(child: child!))`; wait for dependencies that expose types like `ColorScheme`, `TextTheme`, `FloatingActionButtonLocation` to migrate."
    avoid: "Passing `package:material_ui` values (e.g. `ColorScheme`) to a dependency whose API uses `package:flutter/material.dart` types; it does not type-check."
    source: https://docs.flutter.dev/release/breaking-changes/material-ui-and-cupertino-ui

  - id: material-ui-localizations-delegates
    since: "3.47"
    priority: 3
    area: framework
    summary: With `package:material_ui`, `GlobalMaterialLocalizations.delegates` includes the Material, Cupertino and Widgets delegates.
    use: "`MaterialApp(localizationsDelegates: GlobalMaterialLocalizations.delegates, ...)` with `package:material_ui/material_ui.dart`."
    avoid: "Listing `GlobalCupertinoLocalizations.delegate`, `GlobalMaterialLocalizations.delegate`, `GlobalWidgetsLocalizations.delegate` from `flutter_localizations` in a `material_ui` app."
    source: https://docs.flutter.dev/release/breaking-changes/material-ui-and-cupertino-ui

  - id: opengles-render-texture-top-down
    since: "3.47"
    priority: 3
    area: framework
    summary: Impeller's OpenGL ES backend now stores render-to-texture content top-down like Metal and Vulkan, so shaders must not flip Y on OpenGL ES.
    use: "Sample with `uv = FlutterFragCoord().xy / u_size` and no flip; for cross-version code guard with `#if defined(IMPELLER_TARGET_OPENGLES) && !defined(IMPELLER_OPENGLES_UNFLIPPED_DEPRECATED)`."
    avoid: "`#ifdef IMPELLER_TARGET_OPENGLES uv.y = 1.0 - uv.y; #endif` in FragmentShader or Flutter GPU code."
    source: https://docs.flutter.dev/release/breaking-changes/opengles-render-to-texture-top-down

  - id: widget-previews-stable
    since: "3.47"
    priority: 3
    area: tooling
    summary: Flutter Widget Previewer is stable; it caches builds in `.widget_preview/` (now in the app template's .gitignore).
    use: "`import 'package:flutter/widget_previews.dart';` and `@Preview(name: '...')` on a top-level function, static method or public no-required-arg widget constructor; run `flutter widget-preview start`."
    avoid: "`@Preview` on private callbacks or members needing required arguments; `dart:io`/`dart:ffi` or native plugins in previews; committing `.widget_preview/`."
    source: https://docs.flutter.dev/tools/widget-previewer
''',
  'stores.yaml': r'''
# The stores' build minimums (spec §6.4, §12): what Google Play and the App
# Store require of an uploaded app's build, from a date on. Only build
# minimums, never review policies (spec §2.3). Each list is oldest first.
# `since` is YYYY-MM-DD, or YYYY-MM when the store named only the month.
# `formFactor` is set when a requirement applies to one kind of device only.
# Checked against the sources on 2026-10-01.
play:
  targetSdk:
    - value: 34
      since: 2025-08-31
      formFactor: tv
      summary: New Android TV apps and updates must target API level 34 or higher.
      source: https://support.google.com/googleplay/android-developer/answer/11926878
    - value: 36
      since: 2026-08-31
      summary: New apps and app updates must target Android 16 (API level 36) or higher; developers can request an extension to 2026-11-01.
      source: https://developer.android.com/google/play/requirements/target-sdk
    - value: 35
      since: 2026-08-31
      formFactor: wear
      summary: New Wear OS apps and updates must target API level 35 or higher.
      source: https://developer.android.com/google/play/requirements/target-sdk
    - value: 35
      since: 2026-08-31
      formFactor: automotive
      summary: New Android Automotive OS apps and updates must target API level 35 or higher.
      source: https://developer.android.com/google/play/requirements/target-sdk
    - value: 34
      since: 2026-08-31
      formFactor: xr
      summary: New Android XR apps and updates must target API level 34 or higher.
      source: https://support.google.com/googleplay/android-developer/answer/11926878
  pageSize16k:
    - since: 2025-11-01
      summary: New apps and app updates that target Android 15 (API level 35) or higher must support 16 KB memory pages on 64-bit devices.
      source: https://android-developers.googleblog.com/2025/05/prepare-play-apps-for-devices-with-16kb-page-size.html
    - since: 2026-08-01
      formFactor: tv
      summary: Android TV apps must be 64-bit and support 16 KB memory pages.
      source: https://support.google.com/googleplay/android-developer/answer/17492799
    - since: 2026-09-15
      formFactor: wear
      summary: Wear OS apps must be 64-bit and support 16 KB memory pages.
      source: https://support.google.com/googleplay/android-developer/answer/17492799
    - since: 2027-02-01
      summary: App updates that don't support 16 KB memory pages can no longer be released.
      source: https://developer.android.com/guide/practices/page-sizes
appStore:
  xcode:
    - value: "14.1"
      since: 2023-04-25
      summary: iOS and iPadOS apps must be built with Xcode 14.1 and the iOS 16.1 SDK or later.
      source: https://developer.apple.com/news/upcoming-requirements/
    - value: 15
      since: 2024-04-29
      summary: Apps must be built with Xcode 15 and the iOS 17 SDK or later.
      source: https://developer.apple.com/news/upcoming-requirements/
    - value: 16
      since: 2025-04-24
      summary: Apps must be built with Xcode 16 and the iOS 18 SDK or later.
      source: https://developer.apple.com/news/?id=9s0rgdy9
    - value: 26
      since: 2026-04-28
      summary: Apps must be built with Xcode 26 or later, using the iOS 26 SDK or later.
      source: https://developer.apple.com/news/upcoming-requirements/
    - value: 27
      since: 2027-04
      summary: iOS and iPadOS apps must be built with the iOS 27 and iPadOS 27 SDK or later, which ships with Xcode 27.
      source: https://developer.apple.com/news/?id=k1mtkt1k
  iosDeploymentTarget:
    - value: 13
      since: 2026-09-09
      summary: iOS and iPadOS apps uploaded to App Store Connect must target iOS 13 or later.
      source: https://developer.apple.com/news/upcoming-requirements/
    - value: 15
      since: 2027-04
      summary: iOS and iPadOS apps uploaded to App Store Connect must target iOS 15 or later.
      source: https://developer.apple.com/app-store/submitting/
''',
